    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Daniel? You're on the platform. I can hear the rails singing."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_3de2bd087f"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "Tram's live. I'm coming down to you. Containment. Ten minutes."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_2dc12d52d3"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Don't. Please. Not if Marcus sent you."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_54c0a534c0"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "Nobody sent me. I'm coming because you're there."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_3b31d8e2c0"
    },
    {
     "command": "wait",
     "args": [
      "1.5"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Can I tell you something stupid? There's a song. I hum it when I'm frightened. I've hummed it eleven thousand times down here."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_8787642b6a"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "I heard you. In the lift. I knew the tune."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_d7895c9109"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "You couldn't. Evelyn wrote the words. Nobody alive knows them but me."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_310c201b97"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "(singing, barely) Little light, little light... hold the line through the night..."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_3a66590e64"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "(singing, without meaning to) ...if the dark calls your name, it is not me."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_93b4f1c8b1"
    },
    {
     "command": "wait",
     "args": [
      "2.5"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Where did you learn that?"
     ],
     "vo": "mira_78f1030762"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "I don't know. I've always known it. I sang it under the covers when I was small. My mum — the woman who raised me — said I came with it."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_ce01ee1ffd"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Came with it."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_1def589b94"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Daniel. When's your birthday?"
     ],
     "vo": "mira_cecba0a28c"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "Fourteenth of August."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_88bd398663"
    },
    {
     "command": "wait",
     "args": [
      "2"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "...Danny?"
     ],
     "vo": "mira_fab6136266"
    },
    {
     "command": "radio_on",
     "args": [
      "true",
      "107.9"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "wait",
     "args": [
      "0.6"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "look",
     "args": [
      "m",
      "1.6"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "...Mira?"
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_feb0fc893b"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "I carried you up that lift. Two forty-four. You had your hand in my hair the whole way up and you never cried once."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_732fb67fa2"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "I gave you to Ines at the gate. I pinned your name to your blanket, and I told her: don't let them ever bring him back here."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_6285b5f6f3"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "And then I went back down for your mother."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_bae37e6509"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "My mother."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_c67955caa3"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Evelyn. Evelyn Voss. You're her son, Danny. You're Evelyn's boy."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_1a10bd6275"
    },
    {
     "command": "wait",
     "args": [
      "2"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "The file. The birthday. Subject D. I kept telling myself — I kept—"
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_069c757780"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "Look at you. You got so old. You got so tall."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_3ba4123444"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "DANIEL",
      "You haven't aged a day."
     ],
     "vo": "daniel_a8b869bfac"
    },
    {
     "command": "line",
     "args": [
      "MIRA (96.1 MHz)",
      "(a laugh that breaks) It's only been one night, Danny. It's only ever been one night."
     ],
     "vo": "mira_81ab8027a7"
    },
    {
     "command": "radio_on",
     "args": [
      "false"
     ]
    },
    {
     "command": "journal",
     "args": [
      "Mira",
      "She carried me up the lift at 02:44 on the 17th of October 1998. She gave me to the gate guard, Ines Duarte, with my name pinned to my blanket. Then she went back down for my mother.\n\nMy mother was Dr. Evelyn Voss.\n\nAnd she sang it over the radio. The song. Evelyn never once let it go out over the air. Now it has."
     ]
    },
